@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 # Optional live level-editor MCP bridge
 
 This is a modified Sauerbraten source tree with an opt-in local editor bridge.
-An external Python server exposes 20 MCP tools over stdio. The game accepts
+An external Python server exposes 22 MCP tools over stdio. The game accepts
 bounded typed requests on a private Unix socket and applies edits on its main
 thread. MCP is currently supported on Linux, in single-player editing only.
 
@@ -71,7 +71,7 @@ its parent must be private mode 0700 and peers must have the same UID.
 | Purpose | Tools |
 | --- | --- |
 | Observe | editor_state, region_read, entity_list, texture_catalog, mapmodel_catalog |
-| Geometry | geometry_fill, texture_apply, material_apply |
+| Geometry | geometry_fill, geometry_face_set, geometry_vertex_set, texture_apply, material_apply |
 | Entities | entity_create, entity_update, entity_delete |
 | History | history_undo, history_redo |
 | View | camera_set, view_capture |
@@ -92,6 +92,23 @@ texture edits affect the exact requested face or all faces. Entities currently
 support light, playerstart and mapmodel. Generation-bound refs expire on
 delete/history/reload; attached entities/history are rejected.
 
+Face and vertex deformation use absolute integer coordinates in units of
+`grid/8`, not relative mouse gestures. `geometry_face_set` takes four `depths`
+in 0..8 along the selected face axis; negative faces also use absolute depths.
+Their order is (R,C)=00,10,01,11: X faces use Y/Z, Y faces use Z/X and Z faces
+use X/Y. It changes that face of every selected cell. `geometry_vertex_set`
+takes a logical `corner` of three XYZ bits and a local XYZ `position` in 0..8.
+Coincident corners and neighboring cells are not moved implicitly.
+
+Both require existing nonempty leaves exactly matching the selection grid.
+Explicitly fill new cells first; coarser/finer geometry returns
+GEOMETRY_RESOLUTION_MISMATCH. All candidate cubes are checked before modifying
+the world: edge ordering/ranges, three-dimensionality and every native face
+triangle's convexity, independently of cached visibility. Invalid geometry
+returns INVALID_GEOMETRY without changing history or the world. Textures and
+materials are retained. An unchanged request does not consume undo or clear
+redo. Each actual deformation is a distinct shared history step.
+
 Native manual edits and MCP edits share undo/redo. Each RPC is a separate step;
 read-only queries preserve the native editing boundary, selection and focus.
 Pending native drags/onrelease commands return BUSY. camera_set selects
@@ -142,7 +159,7 @@ definitions that cannot be reconstructed can also disable export.
 Mutation budgets: 4096 cells, 65536 visited nodes, 8 MiB snapshot and 16 MiB inverse
 preparation. Reads return at most 256 leaves / 4096 nodes per page. Captures are
 at most 1280x720, with a 10-minute TTL and 64 MiB owned cache. Batch, coop editing,
-vertex/terrain/blend editing and lighting baking are outside this first version.
+terrain/blend editing and lighting baking are outside this first version.
 
 ## Verification
 
